slabs:
It is cold on the terrace;
A pale wind licks along the stone slabs,
But the dog gazes through the glass

slack:
An excellent landlord of the olden stamp,
If somewhat slack in new philanthropies;
Who keeps his birthdays with a tenants’ dance,

Tu'key gobbler gwine 'roun' blowin',
Gwine 'roun' gibbin' sass an' slack;
Keep on talkin', Mistah Tu'key,

slashed:
shattered, cut apart,
slashed open;
though my heels press my own wet life

slackening:
She stood on inner ground that budded flowers;
While circling in their never-slackening round
Danced by the mystic hours.

slant:
No shadow from the sloping fields of yesterday;
For every hour they slant across the hedge a different way,
The shadows are never the same.

slaying:
Born in the battle where fleet Death was flying,
Slaying with sabre-stroke bloody and fell;
Born where the heroes and martyrs were dying,

slain:
While the sixth seeks some gloomy cave in vain,
Struck with the rest, and mingled with the slain.
One only daughter lives, and she the least;

slaughtered:
The roots that work below;
From your rich dust and slaughtered will
A tree with tongues will grow.

slavery's:
Beings once chattles now are men;
Over the gloom of slavery's night,
Has flashed the dawn of freedom's light.
